1
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:24,957
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:27,687
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:37,517
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,917
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,597
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:46,677
So bright, so bold, but so elusive.

9
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:48,697
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:51,857
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,697
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,557
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:05,617
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:08,877
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:11,000
We live in wonder.

17
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,177
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:27,577
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:29,937
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,020 --> 00:01:32,057
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:33,537
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,637
We don't want to live ordinary life.

24
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:39,777
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:42,540
We live in one another.

26
00:01:52,860 --> 00:01:54,960
So now tell me!

27
00:01:57,880 --> 00:01:59,860
Where can I find Crocodile?

28
00:02:05,060 --> 00:02:05,890
Luffy...

29
00:02:05,973 --> 00:02:06,803
Luffy was right.

30
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:08,700
I've made up my mind now.

31
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:10,120
Change of plans.

32
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:12,241
We're going to go find Crocodile.

33
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:13,790
Yeah.

34
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:17,657
That does seem like the quickest way of
stopping the fighting from happening.

35
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:20,197
And we can quit wandering
around the desert, too.

36
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:21,817
That was beginning to get old.

37
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:23,540
So, where is he anyway?

38
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:25,940
This damn Crocodile guy? Let's see.

39
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:30,052
This is the capital city,
Alubarna, where my father rules.

40
00:02:30,140 --> 00:02:34,140
And the rebel army is camped here,
getting ready to invade Alubarna.

41
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:38,613
So we just need to get to Crocodile
before the rebels can get to Alubarna.

42
00:02:39,540 --> 00:02:42,357
This is where Crocodile is. Over here.

43
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:43,300
Rain Base.

44
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:44,640
Rain Base?

45
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:49,218
It's a city a bit to the north of
us, about a day's journey from here.

46
00:02:58,140 --> 00:02:58,970
Okay,

47
00:02:59,053 --> 00:03:00,797
did I or did I not tell the two of you to

48
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:02,577
quit with the pathetic
moaning all the time?

49
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:03,697
Who are you to talk?

50
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:04,797
You get to ride on the damn camel.

51
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:07,877
You could at least let us
ride Eyelash for a little bit.

52
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:09,317
You're a big fat camel hawk.

53
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,297
Get off your high horse.

54
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:13,477
Hey, Chopper, you've managed to
make it all day without collapsing.

55
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:15,266
Yeah, I'm trying hard not to.

56
00:03:16,420 --> 00:03:19,337
Vivi, does this rain-based
city have a water supply?

57
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:21,067
Oh, yeah, no shortage there.

58
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:25,197
It's a gambling town, almost completely
isolated from all the fighting.

59
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:26,260
Ah! Gambling?

60
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:29,687
No way Nami, we're not
going there to gamble.

61
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:33,605
I guess people need some places
to relax, even here in Alabasta.

62
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:35,940
Come, come! No way!

63
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:39,997
Come on, give me some!

64
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:40,910
Come, come!

65
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:42,000
Leave me alone!

66
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:45,921
Come on, Lupe, just give
me one sip of it, please.

67
00:03:46,380 --> 00:03:48,237
Isn't that why he gave it to us?

68
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:50,977
The old guy from the
sandstorm place gave it to me.

69
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:54,119
He had to dig all night
just to get this much of it.

70
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:59,557
We can't just go drinking it like it's
regular water or something, so no way!

71
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:00,470
Wow.

72
00:04:00,553 --> 00:04:02,437
You can restrain yourself sometimes.

73
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:04,640
Well, yeah, of course I can, Nami.

74
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:06,917
That was a rude thing to say, you know.

75
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,360
Take another step. Hey, water.

76
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:12,580
So, how long till rain base, Vivi?

77
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:15,260
Hey, Luffy.

78
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:17,400
Thanks a lot.

79
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:20,617
I never would have been able to
make this decision on my own.

80
00:04:20,700 --> 00:04:22,160
Okay, then give me food.

81
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:26,140
After I beat up Crocodile, give me food.

82
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:27,772
I'll eat till I explode.

83
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:30,080
I promise I will.

84
00:04:44,060 --> 00:04:45,337
Please, Koza!

85
00:04:45,420 --> 00:04:47,479
Just let me join you in the Rebels!

86
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:48,510
I will not.

87
00:04:48,593 --> 00:04:49,500
And why not?

88
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:52,137
Don't I have every right to
be part of the rebellion, too?

89
00:04:52,220 --> 00:04:53,717
I hate the king and the royal army.

90
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:56,157
Just let me fight with
you so I can prove it.

91
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:57,534
Barakla, show the kid.

92
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:03,977
He got that wound trying to protect
me in the middle of a battle.

93
00:05:04,060 --> 00:05:06,697
Would you like to see the medical
tents and the grave sites, too?

94
00:05:06,780 --> 00:05:07,721
It isn't pretty.

95
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:09,600
I'm not scared.

96
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:11,140
You can't scare me!

97
00:05:12,320 --> 00:05:14,397
The cities have dried up
and a lot of people have

98
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:16,617
died because the king stole
all the rain from everyone.

99
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:19,876
My friends got sick because
there wasn't enough water!

100
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:21,689
It's all the King's fault!

101
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:23,217
I only want the chance!

102
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:24,217
Just let me fight!

103
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:26,817
I'm not scared of getting
injured or even dying!

104
00:05:26,900 --> 00:05:30,197
That's where you're different from us
and why I can't let you join our ranks.

105
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:32,457
We're all afraid and
none of us want to fight.

106
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:34,457
Well, why do you fight then, Koza?

107
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:36,317
We don't do it because we want to.

108
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:37,937
We do it because we have to.

109
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:40,337
Because that's what our
country needs us to do.

110
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:44,773
Whether you understand that or not
makes little difference, so just leave.

111
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:48,137
Dammit, I told you to leave now.

112
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:50,985
Battle is no place for
a child, do you hear me?

113
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:55,220
What's wrong, huh?

114
00:05:55,740 --> 00:05:59,377
It's not like you to rant and rave
like that, especially at a kid.

115
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:02,197
It was like looking at
myself when I was his age.

116
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:03,440
It made me angry.

117
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:09,953
And the worst part is I haven't
changed a bit since then.

118
00:06:10,580 --> 00:06:12,557
Have we gathered all
the weapons we require?

119
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:14,740
No, it's proving quite difficult.

120
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:17,797
We need to begin contacting
all the other towns.

121
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:19,697
As soon as we have all the weapons,

122
00:06:19,780 --> 00:06:22,780
we will begin our final
Alto attack on Alubarna.

123
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:29,051
Sire, it's only a matter of time now
before the rebel army attacks Alubarna.

124
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:32,157
We must take action against the
rebels quickly before it's too late.

125
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:33,070
I said no!

126
00:06:33,220 --> 00:06:34,720
We'll not attack them!

127
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:36,737
This is not some little quarrel.

128
00:06:36,820 --> 00:06:38,737
We strike first, they will strike back.

129
00:06:38,820 --> 00:06:42,173
Sire, we are barely clinging
to power right now as it is.

130
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:43,817
That does not matter.

131
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:45,937
I don't care about my rule at the moment.

132
00:06:46,020 --> 00:06:47,717
Ever since the Dance Powder incident,

133
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:50,837
it's been clear that someone's
trying to tear apart our country.

134
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:53,197
Are you suggesting that
we attack our citizens

135
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:55,751
before we determine who's behind all this?

136
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:58,937
Because that would be the true
destruction of our kingdom.

137
00:06:59,020 --> 00:06:59,850
Don't you know?

138
00:06:59,933 --> 00:07:01,312
A country is its people.

139
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:05,029
But sir, whoever is behind this
hasn't shown himself so far.

140
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:08,457
We can't sit back and wait for
this unknown force to divide us.

141
00:07:08,540 --> 00:07:10,417
We must act. Can't you see?

142
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:11,559
Please understand.

143
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:13,040
I can't.

144
00:07:13,580 --> 00:07:16,698
The king will not allow us
to take the offensive now.

145
00:07:16,860 --> 00:07:20,337
We can barely even keep our own
soldiers happy at this point.

146
00:07:20,420 --> 00:07:24,538
I would feel much better if we had
Igaram with us at a time like this.

147
00:07:25,260 --> 00:07:29,337
Igaram has left a note saying that
he's leaving the island for a while.

148
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:33,057
Even as we speak, he and Princess
Vivi are still out there somewhere,

149
00:07:33,140 --> 00:07:35,728
trying hard to figure
out who's behind this.

150
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:37,040
I hope they can.

151
00:07:37,900 --> 00:07:39,537
Chaka! Pal! Come quickly!

152
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:40,620
What is it?

153
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:41,980
It's Karoo!

154
00:07:42,160 --> 00:07:43,577
He's returned to the palace!

155
00:07:43,660 --> 00:07:44,490
Karu's back?

156
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:55,260
We heard, Your Majesty.

157
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:56,795
Who sent that letter?

158
00:07:58,540 --> 00:08:00,000
There's no mistaking it.

159
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,828
It's my Vivi's handwriting.

160
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:03,160
So, Your Majesty.

161
00:08:03,260 --> 00:08:04,157
It means...

162
00:08:04,240 --> 00:08:05,777
Karoo brought news from Vivi.

163
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:06,860
What does it say?

164
00:08:08,820 --> 00:08:09,650
Father.

165
00:08:09,733 --> 00:08:12,597
Everything I've written
here is true beyond a doubt.

166
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:14,680
Please read this letter carefully.

167
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:24,897
I've discovered the identity of the person
who's trying to destroy Alabasta Kingdom.

168
00:08:24,980 --> 00:08:27,720
It is a warlord of the sea, Crocodile.

169
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:36,560
Because of Crocodile, Igaram is dead.

170
00:08:37,040 --> 00:08:39,569
He died as he lived,
a hero to his country.

171
00:08:40,700 --> 00:08:41,660
It's Crocodile.

172
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:44,777
I stupidly thought he was
loyal to the world government.

173
00:08:44,860 --> 00:08:48,277
I never even wondered if he
was the one behind all of this.

174
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:49,740
How could he be dead?

175
00:08:50,640 --> 00:08:54,816
He died as he would have wanted,
protecting Princess Vivi and Alabasta.

176
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:59,637
But now, Father, I have joined forces
with an amazing group of people.

177
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:02,297
They have given me great
confidence and power.

178
00:09:02,380 --> 00:09:04,337
If I continue to work beside them,

179
00:09:04,420 --> 00:09:06,917
I believe we will be able to make
a difference in this country.

180
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,900
We have reason to hope now.

181
00:09:09,480 --> 00:09:11,340
Alabasta can and will be saved.

182
00:09:11,820 --> 00:09:13,349
Please have faith, Father.

183
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:14,500
We can do this.

184
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:16,070
Vivi.

185
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:24,777
Vivi's letter mentions that you
fought very valiantly as well, Karoo.

186
00:09:24,860 --> 00:09:26,080
You served her well.

187
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:28,537
Oh, it looks like you've been hurt.

188
00:09:28,620 --> 00:09:29,450
Let me see.

189
00:09:30,620 --> 00:09:33,796
Okay, no matter what happens
on that island, Remember,

190
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:37,760
this thing on all our arms
is a sign of our friendship!

191
00:09:39,540 --> 00:09:40,370
Chaka!

192
00:09:41,620 --> 00:09:43,326
We know the enemy's identity.

193
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:45,501
Prepare the soldiers to move out.

194
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:49,017
Phoebe's courage and Igaram's
death won't be in vain.

195
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:50,637
We're going to take action now.

196
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:53,000
We'll head for Rainbase and Crocodile.

197
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:55,857
Please do not be so hasty, Your Majesty.

198
00:09:55,940 --> 00:09:58,837
Rainbase is far away and there
are many preparations to be made.

199
00:09:58,920 --> 00:10:02,337
What's more, Crocodile has many of
the citizens firmly on his side.

200
00:10:02,420 --> 00:10:06,200
even more of them than you do,
Sire, with all due respect.

201
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:09,584
If we send forces to
Rainbase now, your majesty,

202
00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:11,797
the rebels will use our absence to attack?

203
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:13,497
and they will take the palace easily.

204
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:14,597
In which case...

205
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:17,677
It doesn't matter if the rebel army
destroys this palace completely.

206
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:19,054
It is only a building.

207
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:22,560
I've told you before, a
country is its people.

208
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:29,517
Even if our royal army does fall in the
end, if we can just defeat Crocodile?

209
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:33,557
this country can still be reborn as
long as its people are safe and whole.

210
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:36,917
If we battle the rebel army
instead, then that will all change.

211
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,471
In that situation, Crocodile's the victor.

212
00:10:39,620 --> 00:10:40,450
Understand?

213
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,030
Majesty.

214
00:10:45,680 --> 00:10:46,640
Yes, I see.

215
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:50,417
For right now, we do not need to
be focusing on the rebel army.

216
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:52,559
We just need to take out Crocodile.

217
00:10:54,420 --> 00:10:57,497
This is one of the seven warlords
of the sea that we're fighting.

218
00:10:57,580 --> 00:10:59,420
He is strong and cunning.

219
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:03,980
There will be many casualties, but we
must accept that and battle onward.

220
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:06,800
Chaka, we need to hold a war council.

221
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:08,434
Assemble the officers.

222
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:11,597
Pell, scout ahead and
conduct reconnaissance.

223
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:12,510
Right.

224
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:16,137
Forgive me for having
underestimated you, Your Majesty.

225
00:11:16,220 --> 00:11:18,300
You are a true man of your country.

226
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:20,818
We head for battle tomorrow morning.

227
00:11:21,780 --> 00:11:24,860
Sir, all soldiers are
to head for rain base.

228
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:37,770
There.

229
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:39,880
So is that the city?

230
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:42,860
That's it?

231
00:11:44,220 --> 00:11:45,460
Are we here?

232
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:48,390
Crocodile.

233
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:49,830
Yeah!

234
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:52,840
Time to kick crocodile's ass!

235
00:11:56,900 --> 00:11:58,500
That's rain base, huh?

236
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:00,997
So after all that's happened,

237
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:03,037
are we operating under the
assumption that Baroque

238
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:05,357
Works knows that we're here
on the island with them?

239
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:06,520
It seems likely.

240
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:07,857
We did run into Mr.

241
00:12:07,940 --> 00:12:08,770
Two,

242
00:12:08,853 --> 00:12:10,137
so I think it's safe to
assume that they have at

243
00:12:10,220 --> 00:12:12,557
least some idea that we
were headed to Alabasta.

244
00:12:12,640 --> 00:12:13,817
Who cares about that?

245
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:15,557
They know exactly what we look like,

246
00:12:15,640 --> 00:12:18,277
so we won't be able to do much of
anything while we're in rain base.

247
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:19,190
Just lay low.

248
00:12:19,273 --> 00:12:20,103
Then why is that?

249
00:12:20,186 --> 00:12:22,417
Because if we get spotted
before we can find Crocodile,

250
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:26,957
I'm sure he can probably come up with all
sorts of nasty ways of taking care of us.

251
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:29,617
Assassination is kind of
their area of expertise.

252
00:12:29,700 --> 00:12:32,280
Laying low, but we're coming, Crocodile!

253
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:34,757
You weren't even listening, were you?

254
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:36,177
Well, no matter what happens,

255
00:12:36,260 --> 00:12:39,897
I will take it upon myself to
protect Nami and Vivi from any harm.

256
00:12:39,980 --> 00:12:42,357
I'm always happy to play Prince Charming.

257
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:44,240
For a lady. Smooth one.

258
00:12:44,620 --> 00:12:46,267
Smoother than you are, Zoro!

259
00:12:46,980 --> 00:12:48,560
I need water.

260
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,740
There is none. Let it go.

261
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:53,600
Water... I'm going!

262
00:12:54,420 --> 00:12:55,860
Wait for me, move me!

263
00:12:56,140 --> 00:12:58,787
Hey, you might want to
take some money along.

264
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:10,677
Captain Smoker, why do you
think that they'll be here?

265
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:13,637
What reason would the Straw Hats
have for coming to Rain Base?

266
00:13:13,720 --> 00:13:15,308
Let's just call it a hunch.

267
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:18,230
Yeah!

268
00:13:18,313 --> 00:13:19,360
Finally we can get water!

269
00:13:20,560 --> 00:13:23,297
I can't put my finger on
it, but something stinks.

270
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:26,457
I just feel like there's something
big lurking in the shadows.

271
00:13:26,540 --> 00:13:28,057
Hey, old lady, give us some water, King!

272
00:13:28,140 --> 00:13:28,970
Yeah, yeah!

273
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:29,910
A whole barrel!

274
00:13:29,993 --> 00:13:30,937
No, we want more than that!

275
00:13:31,020 --> 00:13:31,961
My barrel, yeah!

276
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:35,097
So then you really do believe that
there is some sort of a connection

277
00:13:35,180 --> 00:13:39,217
between the Baroque Works Crime
Organization and the Straw Hats crew?

278
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:40,130
Water!

279
00:13:43,340 --> 00:13:47,437
The only thing I know for sure is that
Straw Hat is out to get Crocodile,

280
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:49,696
one of the Seven Warlords of the Sea.

281
00:13:51,820 --> 00:13:53,360
This is about forever!

282
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:57,299
We need to hurry up and get
our marks on the others!

283
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:17,871
I'm going to go use the little boys' room.

284
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:21,337
Do you really think we can count
on them to stay out of trouble?

285
00:14:21,420 --> 00:14:23,837
Even they can handle little errands, okay?

286
00:14:23,920 --> 00:14:25,200
Right? I don't know.

287
00:14:25,460 --> 00:14:27,097
I'll bet they managed
to screw something up.

288
00:14:27,180 --> 00:14:28,560
It is Usopp and Luffy.

289
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:30,897
I'd start getting ready
to run if I were you.

290
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:32,460
Run away! Yeah!

291
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:33,799
Protect the water!

292
00:14:33,940 --> 00:14:34,770
Right!

293
00:14:34,853 --> 00:14:35,777
Dammit, we're going after them.

294
00:14:35,860 --> 00:14:37,720
Get the marines to Shoujou. Sir!

295
00:14:38,260 --> 00:14:39,090
Oh, right.

296
00:14:39,173 --> 00:14:40,357
How much do I owe you?

297
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:44,597
If you know those brats, you'd better
add all the water they took to your tab.

298
00:14:44,680 --> 00:14:45,510
Of course.

299
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:46,480
I'm so sorry.

300
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:48,816
What are the damn marines doing here?

301
00:14:51,340 --> 00:14:52,634
How could I know that?

302
00:14:52,780 --> 00:14:54,662
Let's just keep running for now!

303
00:14:56,740 --> 00:14:57,620
You win.

304
00:14:57,800 --> 00:14:59,877
Looks like the Marines are chasing them.

305
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:00,860
No way!

306
00:15:01,220 --> 00:15:03,632
So why are those idiots running this way?

307
00:15:03,940 --> 00:15:06,528
Hey, Tony hasn't made
his way back here yet.

308
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:07,450
He'll be fine.

309
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:09,197
Chopper can manage on his own.

310
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:11,617
Hey, you guys, I think the teams are here!

311
00:15:11,700 --> 00:15:12,530
Hey, thank you!

312
00:15:12,613 --> 00:15:14,157
We hadn't noticed that, Luffy!

313
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:15,070
Hurry it up!

314
00:15:15,153 --> 00:15:16,880
We can't lose them this time, men!

315
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:21,480
Those idiots sure can run.

316
00:15:21,580 --> 00:15:23,168
I'll give them that anyway.

317
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:25,060
This is bad!

318
00:15:25,560 --> 00:15:28,560
Brokeworks will see us, if
we run through the city!

319
00:15:34,660 --> 00:15:37,097
I think it's a little
too late for that, Usopp.

320
00:15:37,180 --> 00:15:39,460
Then it's decided! Let's go! Huh?

321
00:15:39,860 --> 00:15:42,960
Wherever Crocodile is,
how about it? Ready?

322
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:48,584
Do you see that building up ahead
with the alligator on its roof?

323
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:51,155
That's the casino that Crocodile runs!

324
00:15:51,500 --> 00:15:53,020
It's called Rain Dinners!

325
00:15:53,560 --> 00:15:54,580
I see it.

326
00:15:54,860 --> 00:15:56,760
So that's where Crocodile is.

327
00:15:58,120 --> 00:16:00,480
It'll be better if we all split up now.

328
00:16:00,700 --> 00:16:02,097
Yeah, it's looking that way.

329
00:16:02,180 --> 00:16:03,010
Right!

330
00:16:03,093 --> 00:16:03,923
See you later!

331
00:16:04,280 --> 00:16:05,110
Right!

332
00:16:07,660 --> 00:16:09,180
Don't die! They split up!

333
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:10,301
Don't lose them!

334
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:12,220
Smokey! Hey!

335
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:15,048
You've got some real
nerve there, Straw Hat.

336
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:17,278
But don't think you can run forever!

337
00:16:17,820 --> 00:16:18,780
White vine!

338
00:16:35,340 --> 00:16:36,660
Ah, too close.

339
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:41,270
Damn.

340
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:42,820
Damn it.

341
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:44,420
Oh, no.

342
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:45,780
Look, over there.

343
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:48,480
It's them, all right.

344
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:50,597
No doubt. Kill them.

345
00:16:50,680 --> 00:16:53,445
It looks like it's the
Baroque work's millions.

346
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:57,577
Well, then I guess we're stuck
between a rock and a hard place, huh?

347
00:16:57,660 --> 00:16:58,660
Go on without me.

348
00:16:59,140 --> 00:16:59,970
Hurry!

349
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:00,970
Okay.

350
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:04,880
Hey, Usak!

351
00:17:05,860 --> 00:17:08,120
You look after Nami. Why?

352
00:17:08,780 --> 00:17:09,610
Just do it.

353
00:17:09,693 --> 00:17:11,445
I'll take care of the Marines.

354
00:17:12,460 --> 00:17:14,960
Okay, I'm on it. But Sanji! Just go!

355
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:20,146
Without that smoke freak around,
they should be easy to handle.

356
00:17:21,700 --> 00:17:22,820
Terribly sorry.

357
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:36,697
I hope Mr.

358
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:38,309
Bushido will be all right.

359
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:45,960
Is that all really pathetic?

360
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:50,640
Roronoa Zoro, I knew we'd meet again.

361
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:53,360
That voice.

362
00:17:54,880 --> 00:17:56,409
I've been looking for you.

363
00:17:56,500 --> 00:17:59,597
What do you think you're doing carelessly
cutting down civilians like that?

364
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:00,977
That's low even for you.

365
00:18:01,060 --> 00:18:03,417
Look, I have my own reasons
for doing it, all right?

366
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:06,937
Besides, I have absolutely no desire
whatsoever to fight you again.

367
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:09,560
We settled our dispute fine in Longtown.

368
00:18:09,840 --> 00:18:10,760
We did not.

369
00:18:11,100 --> 00:18:12,041
I'm not through.

370
00:18:12,180 --> 00:18:13,797
I haven't even dealt you a single blow.

371
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:16,660
Duh, she looked way too much like her!

372
00:18:17,060 --> 00:18:19,777
And put that damn face
of yours away, will you?

373
00:18:19,860 --> 00:18:21,160
What did you say?

374
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:22,460
You're insulting me?

375
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:24,397
That's a really pathetic tactic.

376
00:18:24,480 --> 00:18:25,560
I'll make you pay!

377
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:28,800
Uh-uh, she's the one
person I can't handle!

378
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:31,300
Hold it!

379
00:18:35,780 --> 00:18:37,580
Get back here, you rats!

380
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:46,327
It's two of them, all right.

381
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:51,150
We're...

382
00:18:51,233 --> 00:18:52,063
we're okay!

383
00:18:52,146 --> 00:18:53,340
Way to go, Usopp!

384
00:18:53,700 --> 00:18:54,860
Look, up ahead!

385
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:56,877
It's the entrance to Rain Dinners!

386
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:59,725
And it looks like it's
in the middle of a lake!

387
00:19:02,060 --> 00:19:02,890
What?

388
00:19:02,973 --> 00:19:03,819
No one's here yet?

389
00:19:03,960 --> 00:19:05,431
All right, let's get him!

390
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:07,100
Like fish in a barrel!

391
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:08,840
No, we're screwed!

392
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:11,390
It's Zoro!

393
00:19:11,473 --> 00:19:14,177
Hold on, I thought Vivi was
supposed to be with you.

394
00:19:14,260 --> 00:19:15,090
She was!

395
00:19:15,173 --> 00:19:16,617
Are you saying she's not here?

396
00:19:16,700 --> 00:19:19,277
Not yet, but maybe she
just went inside already.

397
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:20,654
Yeah, let's go in too.

398
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:23,990
Loopy!

399
00:19:24,073 --> 00:19:24,903
Get back here!

400
00:19:24,986 --> 00:19:25,816
It's that smoker guy.

401
00:19:25,899 --> 00:19:26,977
Hey, you guys, let's go!

402
00:19:27,060 --> 00:19:28,600
We have to run inside now!

403
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:31,720
Right behind you!

404
00:19:33,520 --> 00:19:34,760
So he's in there!

405
00:19:35,160 --> 00:19:37,297
Then I guess that's where I'm going!

406
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:41,460
Oh, Phoebe and the pirates
are in town paying us a visit.

407
00:19:41,820 --> 00:19:45,702
Yes, we just received word from
the millions that they've arrived.

408
00:19:55,160 --> 00:19:59,200
Let's be sure to welcome
them very warmly. Yes.

409
00:20:02,420 --> 00:20:03,820
Listen up, crocodile!

410
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:07,940
I'm coming for you, and I'm
about to kick your sandy ass!

411
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:09,200
Get ready!
